Dang, sorry about the missing data.  I had included it because that's involved in driving differences in the y axis.  Pre-computing those for the fronts may be doable for a single species but there's way more data than that IRL.  It feels like a ginormous hack, since I'd have to come up with values for 3 species x 3 years, then I'd still need to be able to find the correct column from inside the function.  It just seems reasonable to me to have some way to reference the axis in relative terms from within the panel.

