Coming up with values over 3 species and 3 years is just adding one more element to the group_by(). It's really not so difficult.

Do you have a more complete dataset we could check it on?

all.fronts <-
cewall %>%          # start with cewall

group_by(year, species) %>%  # group by year and species

summarise(quartermoths= 0.75 * max(avgmoths, na.rm=TRUE)) %>%  # compute 75% of the maximum moths
full_join(all.fronts, .)  # join this data back to all.fronts so you can use it in ggplot

These should plot just fine.

B

